<task id="063" project="messaging-communication-app-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Bidirectional inline content quoting (email↔message) via the channel-agnostic `sprk_body`</title>
    <phase>W6 — UI (polling timeline + PCF accessories)</phase>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <estimated-hours>5</estimated-hours>
    <dependencies>060</dependencies>
    <blocks></blocks>
    <tags>frontend, communication</tags>
    <rigor-hint>FULL</rigor-hint>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies shared `@spaarke/ui-components` `.tsx`/`.ts` (the timeline compose box + EmailComposer prefill path) to add a cross-channel "quote into…" action in both directions; touches the send-side authoring surface consumed by every message + email composer. Fluent v9 (ADR-021) + shared-lib (ADR-012) bind; correctness of the quote-format seam matters. FULL per the frontend-shared-lib bar (mirrors email-r4 020/023 FULL).</rigor-reason>
    <parallel-group>W6</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>All-client TypeScript in `src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/**`; disjoint from 061 (PCF packaging) and 062 (accessory wiring) file surfaces. Depends on 060 (the compose box + composer prefill path it extends).</parallel-reason>
    <fr-refs>FR-13</fr-refs>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <effort>high</effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Add **bidirectional inline content quoting** between email and message, both directions, via the channel-agnostic `sprk_body`/`sprk_bodyformat` (FR-13, design §6.3):

    - **"Quote into message"** — from an email (or any `sprk_communication` row), read its `sprk_body` + `sprk_bodyformat`, format the content as an **inline quote**, and prefill the MESSAGE composer (the timeline compose box, task 060) with it.
    - **"Quote into email"** — from a message row, read its `sprk_body`, format as an inline quote, and prefill the EMAIL composer (`<EmailComposer/>` in reply/compose mode).

    This is a **read → format → prefill** operation, NOT an extraction — because `sprk_body` is the channel-agnostic body on every message, no `.eml` parsing is required (that is only needed for byte-exact forwarding with original attachments, which is out of R1 scope). Net-new = a "quote into…" action affordance + a shared quote-formatting helper (`quoteBody(sourceBody, sourceFormat, targetFormat)`) that produces inline-quoted content (e.g., `>`-prefixed / blockquote), respecting the target composer's body format.

    Wire the action into both composer surfaces: the timeline compose box (message target) and the `<EmailComposer/>` prefill path (email target). Keep the quote helper channel-agnostic and pure (unit-testable). Fluent v9 (ADR-021); shared-lib rules (ADR-012); no client-side ACS SDK (NFR-04 — this is pure Dataverse-body reformatting).
  </prompt>

  <role>
    React 18 + TypeScript developer fluent in Fluent UI v9 and the shipped `<EmailComposer/>` prefill/mode helpers (`deriveReplyState`, body-format handling) + the task-060 timeline compose box. Comfortable authoring a small pure formatting helper reused by both composer surfaces.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A "quote into message" action prefills the timeline message composer with an inline-quoted email body, and a "quote into email" action prefills the email composer with an inline-quoted message body — both directions, driven by a shared pure `quoteBody(...)` helper honoring the target body format, with no `.eml` parsing and no ACS SDK. Fluent v9 compliant; `npm run build` + `npm run lint` clean; the helper is unit-tested.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Design §6.3: cross-channel content reuse is a read-format-prefill operation because `sprk_body` is the channel-agnostic body. Both directions ship in R1. The net-new surface is a "quote into…" action + quote formatting; no `.eml` parsing is needed.

      §11 Component Justification: the quote helper is a single shared function reused by both composer surfaces — it does NOT overlap any existing helper (the `<EmailComposer/>` `deriveReplyState`/`deriveForwardState` derive same-channel reply/forward state; this is CROSS-channel body quoting into a fresh composer prefill). The concrete failure mode without it is FR-13 unmet: content cannot move between channels as inline quoted text. Extension over new: reuse the composer's existing prefill/initial-body props (task 060 kept the compose box prefill prop-driven for exactly this) rather than adding a second prefill mechanism.

      No ACS SDK, no BFF publish-size/CVE (this is client-only body reformatting reading persisted `sprk_body` already available to the composer/timeline).
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CommunicationTimeline/subcomponents/TimelineComposeBox.tsx (UPDATE — accept quoted-content prefill + "quote into message" action)</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/EmailComposer/EmailComposer.tsx (READ/UPDATE — prefill path for "quote into email")</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CommunicationTimeline/subcomponents/MessageRow.tsx (UPDATE — "quote into email" affordance per row)</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/utils/quoteBody.ts (NEW — pure quote-formatting helper)</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/EmailComposer/EmailComposer.reducer.ts (READ — deriveReplyState/body-format handling to mirror)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="FR-13">"Quote into message" and "quote into email" read the source `sprk_body`/`sprk_bodyformat` and prefill the target composer as inline quoted content, both directions — without `.eml` parsing.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">Fluent UI v9 only for any action affordance; semantic tokens; dark mode via host `FluentProvider`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-012">Shared-library rules — the quote helper + composer edits live in `@spaarke/ui-components`; export the helper via the barrel; no fork.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-04">No client-side ACS SDK — this is pure Dataverse-body reformatting; no `@azure/communication-*` import.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The quote helper `quoteBody(sourceBody, sourceFormat, targetFormat)` is PURE + channel-agnostic + unit-tested; respect the target composer's body format (HTML blockquote vs plain-text `>`-prefix).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">§11 — reuse the composer's existing prefill/initial-body props (task 060 kept it prop-driven); do NOT add a second prefill mechanism. No `.eml` parsing (out of R1 scope).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">No BFF publish-size / CVE (client only, root §10 N/A). Build via `npm run build` (dev).</constraint>
  </constraints>

