  <steps>
    <step order="1">Read design §6.3, spec FR-13, the `<EmailComposer/>` reducer prefill/`deriveReplyState` + body-format handling, and the task-060 `TimelineComposeBox` prefill prop + `MessageRow`.</step>
    <step order="2">Author the pure helper `src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/utils/quoteBody.ts`: `quoteBody(sourceBody, sourceFormat, targetFormat)` → inline-quoted content (HTML `&lt;blockquote&gt;` when target is HTML; `>`-prefixed lines when target is plain text), with optional attribution line (sender/date). Channel-agnostic; no ACS/`.eml` dependency. Export via the shared-lib barrel.</step>
    <step order="3">Wire "quote into message": add an action affordance (Fluent v9) on an email/`sprk_communication` row (or the timeline) that calls `quoteBody(...)` and sets the timeline compose box's prefill prop (message composer prefilled).</step>
    <step order="4">Wire "quote into email": add a "quote into email" affordance on a message `MessageRow` that calls `quoteBody(...)` and prefills `<EmailComposer/>` (reply/compose mode) via its initial-body/prefill path.</step>
    <step order="5">Confirm both directions honor the target body format and that no `.eml` parsing is introduced; grep-verify no `@azure/communication-*` import.</step>
    <step order="6">Write unit tests for `quoteBody(...)`: HTML-target produces a blockquote; plain-text-target produces `>`-prefixed lines; empty/whitespace source handled; format round-trip (email→message→email) is stable enough for inline quoting.</step>
    <step order="7">Run `npm run build` + `npm run lint` in `@spaarke/ui-components`; both clean.</step>
    <step order="9.5">FULL-rigor quality gates: `code-review` (focus: pure helper, no second prefill path, no `.eml` parsing, no ACS import, Fluent v9 tokens); `adr-check` against ADR-021/ADR-012 + `spec.md` (FR-13, NFR-04, §11 reuse). Address Critical + High findings.</step>
    <step order="10">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md` (063 ✅) + `current-task.md`; record decisions (quote-format representation, attribution-line shape, which composer prefill props were reused).</step>
  </steps>

